   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["v", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a02652ba-e65a-4b01-ad8b-3612d14d190e"],
 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "draws a transverse light clock carried by the observer of velocity ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ", with ",
 StyleBox["n", "TI"],
 " bounces between the observer and a mirror.",
 "\n",
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"79bc9b28-55b7-44e9-aeaf-803be264e82e"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["LightClockConstruction"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraCausality/ref/LightClockConstruction", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraCausality Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   StyleBox["v", "TI"], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f5e23146-4962-4965-8e13-143968e80ea2"],
 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "draws 8 bounces."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"21522900-0b3b-403d-b986-6caa918550e4"],

Cell["\<\
Experimental: figure. The figure's layout and options may change.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"b6026d9a-d44f-4402-ad7b-aafd4850e4b1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Definition: the observer of velocity ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 " (red) carries a mirror on the parallel worldline (faint red) at the \
Euclidean distance ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<ClockLength\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8cdfb513-b4e7-436a-a878-737d78f066db"],
 " along the unit normal ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["cos",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"-", 
     StyleBox["sin",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]}]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "99991d47-dce6-4a85-b737-d7fd9e0a33ee"],
 " of the worldline, \[Alpha] = ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["WorldlineAngle"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraCausality/ref/WorldlineAngle", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraCausality Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["v", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["\[CurlyPhi]", "TR"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a75140ba-c0e6-4977-82a3-f11f2b308be9"],
 ". Light leaves the observer at arc length ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<StartArcLength\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3f997b9d-554b-41fc-9239-d8f03bddf224"],
 ", runs along the light direction ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["sin",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", "\[CurlyPhi]"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["cos",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", "\[CurlyPhi]"}]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d9673ec3-7a6d-49d4-94c4-1ec63397199b"],
 " to the mirror and back along ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"-", 
     StyleBox["sin",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", "\[CurlyPhi]"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["cos",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", "\[CurlyPhi]"}]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "99f95e97-640c-4dad-91cf-1e65f953b97e"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["n", "TI"],
 " segments in all; each return to the observer (purple) is one tick. Because \
the two worldlines are parallel, every round trip is the same translate along \
the worldline, so the ticks are equally spaced in the observer's proper time; \
the rest observer (faint blue) sees the period \[Gamma] times longer in radar \
time. At ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 " = 0 the figure is the clock at rest."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"fddfc4c6-47a2-4f0b-ae51-bc6502df76d1"],

